  "conclusion": "On the clean, lexically disjoint corr-binary-occupation \u2192 eng-french transfer, direct family comparison gives gemma: SSAE leads (SSAE JumpReLU (penalized) versus SAE ReLU (penalized), SSAE\u2212SAE +0.0071), pythia: SSAE leads (SSAE TopK (penalized) versus SAE JumpReLU (penalized), SSAE\u2212SAE +0.0003). Across all source regimes the lead counts are gemma: best-family SSAE 3, SAE 0, ties 0, pythia: best-family SSAE 2, SAE 1, ties 0. Matched-activation counts are gemma: matched nonlinear SSAE 8, SAE 1, ties 0, pythia: matched nonlinear SSAE 4, SAE 5, ties 0; LLMs are not pooled. The legacy corr-binary regime remains a pair-mixture diagnostic because its household vocabulary overlaps the target.",
  "entry_point": "experiments.exp04.report",
  "experiment_id": "exp04",
  "figures": [
